    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d137">

                <pb facs="0251" n="189" xml:id="pg189"/>

                <head>No. 132.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Noyes to Mr. Evarts</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1878-10-11"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 11, 1878</date>.
                        (Received October 25.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 153.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose an additional
                    list of the names of contributors to the fund in aid of the sufferers from
                    yellow fever in America.</p>
                <p>It will be observed with satisfaction that the French people, members of the
                    cabinet and others, including distinguished names, have responded liberally to
                    the sufferings of our country-people. The generosity has been spontaneous and
                    unsolicited.</p>
                <p>Before this dispatch reaches the State Department, a considerable sum of money
                    will have been forwarded to you in addition to the amount heretofore
                    transmitted.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>EDWARD F. NOYES.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d137-a1.xml" xpointer="d137-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
